    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6269" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">callaïs</span></b> , ĭdis,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλλαΐς</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a sea-green precious
				stone</i>, <i>the turquoise</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 37,
				10, 56, § 151</span></i> (in <i><span class="en">Sol.
			20</span></i> called callaica).—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">callăĭnus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>turquoisecolored</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lacernae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					14, 139</span></i>
			.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">callăĭna</span></b> ,
			ae, f., <i>a precious stone
				of a pale-green color</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin.
				37, 8, 33, § 110 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">37, 10, 54, §
			147</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">id. 37, 10, 56, § 151</span></i>. </div>
